      "writtenOn": "2023-07-21T14:23:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discussed offline at length with Sam, we will very slightly change the logic so that if we have \n```\nC --------\u003e B (exports: NO) ------------\u003e A (exports: YES)\n    libs                    static_libs     \n```\nthen C will see A\u0027s proguard flags.\n\nWe can then simplify the provider to only have 2 depsets, one \"unconditionally exported\" set, and one set that represents the flags that this module would use if R8 needed to be run on it (\"static\").\n\nThe logic is then, if exports:YES, unconditional set \u003d static set \u003d this module\u0027s flag + its libs unconditional sets + its static libs static sets. If exports:NO, unconditional_set \u003d its libs unconditional sets, static \u003d this module\u0027s flag + its libs unconditional sets + its static libs static sets.\n\nWe\u0027ll right a bunch of small unit tests with 3 modules like above with all relevant combinations of `libs`, `static_libs`, exports yes/no to make the logic clearer",
